  "instance_name": "shared_mischievous_deception",
  "label": "Shared mischievous deception as humor",
  "description": "The humor of the meme hinges on the concept of shared deception — where two people conspire to pretend something is true (no donuts left) when it’s actually false (there are two). This is a common comedic device in everyday life and media, often used to create relatable, lighthearted moments. The meme’s effectiveness depends on the audience recognizing this type of social interaction as humorous.",
